# Roslyn Analyzers

Roslyn diagnostics (CA*, IDE*, VSTHRD*, RS*) are not JetBrains inspections. `run-jetbrains-inspectcode.ps1` will not catch them.

Three analyzer packages feed this gate, all referenced in `Directory.Build.props`: `Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.NetAnalyzers` (CA/IDE), `Microsoft.VisualStudio.Threading.Analyzers` (VSTHRD — sync-over-async, blocking calls), and `Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.BannedApiAnalyzers` (RS0030 — symbols listed in `BannedSymbols.txt`).

## When to run

After creating or materially editing any `.cs` file, and before marking a Spec Kit task complete or finishing implementation work, run:

```powershell
./scripts/run-roslyn-analyzers.ps1
```

From the repository root. Use `-BaseRef <base>` when the base branch is not the repo default.

Run alongside InspectCode and cyclomatic complexity — all three are required.

## Failure handling

- **Exit `1`** — fix every reported CA/IDE warning before proceeding.
- **Exit `2` (SKIPPED)** — nothing was analysed, usually because no `.cs` file changed against the base branch. It is not a pass. When you need verification rather than a diff check, re-run with `-All`.
- CA1502 is excluded from this script; use `run-cyclomatic-complexity.ps1` for complexity.
- Severities are configured in `.editorconfig` under the Roslyn analyzer gate section.
- To ban an API outright (e.g. `DateTime.Now`), add it to `BannedSymbols.txt` as `P:|M:|T:|F:<DocumentationCommentId>;<reason>` rather than writing a new rule.

## Explicit file scope

```powershell
./scripts/run-roslyn-analyzers.ps1 -Files "path/to/File.cs"
```

## Full solution scan

```powershell
./scripts/run-roslyn-analyzers.ps1 -All
```
